  "behavior_findings": [
    "AIInit accepts window,RDRAM,AI-register-bank,MI-register-bank,event-mask arguments; the later six-argument interface adds other state. It creates a0x40000-byte secondary buffer and one event at byte offset0x3ffff.",
    "AIPlay copies the pending guest block into the end of this buffer, sets the playback cursor to0x3ffff minus its length, and starts non-looping playback. Four global Lock outputs are subsequently supplied to Unlock.",
    "TAudioEvents derives from TThread. Its worker waits up to100ms for the completion event, clears the playing Boolean, advances the queued address/length register pair, calls AIPlay for the next block, clears the busy bit and signals the emulator event mask when enabled.",
    "AIGetLen returns0x40000 minus the write-cursor result from GetCurrentPosition, or zero when disabled/uninitialized. The temporary cursor itself is stack-local.",
    "AISetBitRate is an actual one-byte RET implementation. AISetDacRate passes the bank field at+0x18 directly to IDirectSoundBuffer::SetFrequency. No later divider/cache-state layout is inferred.",
    "TDSSecondaryBuffer has an8-byte instance (VMT pointer plus COM interface). TAudioEvents has a40-byte instance. These are heap object instances, distinct from their4-byte global pointer slots.",
    "Unit lifecycle counters near the application state arise in Delphi initialization/finalization routines. They cannot be treated as retained application declarations in a later C translation unit.",
    "The default secondary-buffer format is16-bit stereo PCM at8000Hz. The helper separately supports a primary format set from caller arguments, but the observed AIInit cooperative-level1 skips that primary-buffer path."
  ],
  "ancestry_assessment": [
    "The archive establishes an earlier DirectSound implementation before the WaveOut0.7/0.7a branch, but does not establish source continuity into the2001 C DirectSound driver.",
    "The four lock outputs, notification record, event/thread/object pointers and helper HRESULT are real historical roles. No surviving name, stable field order, or same object extent ties any of them to a particular anonymous2001/2003 interval.",
    "Only broad interface behavior such as DummyMode and guest AI/MI register updates is shared. That behavior does not justify assigning names or types to the later44 anonymous strong-state bytes.",
    "No new storage declaration is supported for promotion. The persistent later holes remain unresolved; no unchanged-compiler or address-masked byte-exact claim is made."
  ],
